findings.finding:
The kernel's `BusinessCalendar` takes `holidays: Map<Year, Set<LocalDate>>` and knows `coveredYears`. Tenancy's HOLIDAY_LIST is one effective-dated value resolved at one `validAt`:
(a) next year's holidays entered as a future-dated value (the §5.7 example) are invisible to a calendar resolved now, so deadlines crossing the year boundary come out wrong;
(b) a year that is configured but has no holidays cannot be told apart from an unconfigured year;
(c) most-specific-wins replaces the whole list, so any TENANT value hides the pack's yearly Eid updates without warning;
(d) `BusinessCalendar.of` failures (NoBusinessDayInWeek, HolidayOutsideItsYear) and a context with no facility, and so no zone, have no `Resolution` variant;
(e) one `Provenance` cannot describe a value built from two settings plus the zone, which tasks needs ('the calendar version it used').

The key grammar `[a-z][a-z0-9-]*` with 'the first segment naming the owner's area' is broken by sibling and own keys:
- tasks' `tasks.orphan.alarmLimit`, `tasks.timers.tickInterval` (camelCase);
- tenancy's own `calendar.*` (owner platform-tenancy);
- config's `flag.<flag key>` (owner e.g. `cds`).
Tenancy's example `platform.tasks.orphan-alarm.max-delay` and §5.11 do not match tasks' key `tasks.orphan.alarmLimit`.

The event names contradict `docs/specs/events/catalogue.md` §4:
- the catalogue's EnterpriseNodeCreated/Changed/Retired vs tenancy's HierarchyNodeCreated/Updated/Moved/Retired;
- SettingChanged vs SettingValueChanged/SettingLockApplied/SettingLockRemoved;
- ChangeSetApplied, BundlePromoted, BundlePromotionRefused, FeatureFlagChanged vs config's ConfigChangeSet*, ConfigBundleActivated/Refused, FlagChanged.
The code registry must equal the catalogue (`UnitTest:event-catalogue-matches-document`).
